    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    The letter informs Vita Sackville-West that M. Bernard Crepin has inquired about the French translation rights to All Passion Spent.
                    The sender has told him that she manages her own translation rights and is forwarding his letter for her to respond directly.
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <placeName>
                            Kent
                        </placeName>
                        <date when="1950-01-23">
                            23rd January, 1950
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName>Vita Sackville-West</persName>                            
                        </addrLine>                        
                    </address>
                    <salute>
                        Dear <persName>Miss Sackville-West</persName>,
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    I am enclosing a letter<note><p>The Modernist Archives Publishin Project holds the letter metioned from Crepin to Aline Burch - MS 2750/410/69.</p></note> asking <lb/>
                    about the French rights in <emph rend="underlined"><title key="novel">All Passion <lb/>
                            Spent</title></emph><note><p>A novel by Vita Sackville-West, which addresses people's place in society, society's constrictions on people, and women's control of their lives (1931).</p></note>/note> from <persName key="MAPP0051">M. Bernard Crepin</persName>. I have <lb/>
                    written telling him that you handle <lb/>
                    translation rights yourself and that I <lb/>
                    am forwarding his letter. Perhaps you <lb/>
                    would be good enough to give him the <lb/>
                    information he requires.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>
                        Yours sincerely,
                    </salute>                                   
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <orgName key="Q1623362">The Hogarth Press Ltd.</orgName>
                        </addrLine>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName>The Hon. V. Sackville-West</persName>
                        </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Sissinghurst Castle,</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Kent</addrLine>                                             
                        </address>                   
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
